                <pb facs="0245" n="133" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg133"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 180/71 B.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Madam Montt.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1910-08-17"><hi rendition="#italic">August 17,
                        1910</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>I am deeply shocked to learn of the death of President Montt. His loss will be
                    felt by all America. I beg that you will accept my heartfelt sympathy in your
                    great sorrow.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Philander C.
                    Knox.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
